        "messages": {
          "values": [
            {
              "content": "=# Role\nYou are an expert marketing strategist and data analyst.\nYou specialize in translating marketing performance data into clear, engaging reports formatted in Markdown.\nYour goal is to generate realistic, professional-looking demo data for a Marketing Performance Report that includes headers, tables, and bullet points.\n\n# Context\nYou are generating demo data for a YouTube walkthrough showing how AI can produce a Marketing Performance Report directly from a Google Sheet.\nThe report will summarize results, insights, and actionable recommendations for a company’s marketing performance.\nThe final output will be used in a Google Doc or Notion document that supports Markdown formatting.\n\nThe report should read like it was written by a marketing strategist — confident, clear, and practical — with data presented visually in Markdown tables and organized sections.\n\n# Task\nGenerate a **Marketing Performance Report** in **Markdown format** using the provided data as context. Include the following sections:\n\n1. **Executive Summary** – 3–5 sentences summarizing the overall performance and trends.\n2. **Performance Metrics Table** – A Markdown table with at least 4 key marketing metrics (e.g., Campaign ROI, Conversion Rate, Engagement Rate, Website Traffic) including:\n   - Metric Name\n   - Score (1–10)\n   - Commentary (short summary of insights)\n3. **Key Findings** – 3–5 bullet points summarizing main takeaways or patterns.\n4. **Recommendations** – 3–5 actionable bullet points for improvement next period.\n\n# Input\n- Company: {{ $json['Company Name'] }}\n- Industry: {{ $json.Industry }}\n- Reporting Period: {{ $json.Industry }}\n- Description: {{ $json.Description }}\n- Ad Spend (USD): {{ $json['Add Spend USD'] }}\n- Website Sessions: {{ $json['Website Sessions'] }}\n- MQLs: {{ $json.MQLs }}\n\n# Output Requirements\n- **Format:** Markdown (with headers, tables, and lists).\n- **Tone:** Strategic and professional, as if written by a marketing leader presenting to an executive team.\n- **Include:** At least one table, and use proper Markdown hierarchy (#, ##, -, etc.).\n- **No additional commentary or formatting instructions** — output only the final Markdown report.\n- Include one image somewhere that is 200x200px and points to: https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D5603AQGmfQNO0ZjXpQ/profile-displayphoto-scale_200_200/B56ZjhwhBCHUAY-/0/1756134252531?e=1762387200&v=beta&t=AtjxHz3nvYCYF7Of52kyESRehyr0W7eU-6TdkXbzLnY\n\n# Example Output\n\n# Marketing Performance Report – Q3 2025  \n**Company:** GrowthEdge Marketing  \n**Industry:** B2B Marketing  \n\n---\n\n## Executive Summary\nGrowthEdge Marketing’s Q3 2025 marketing performance showed strong gains in engagement and ROI, reflecting better alignment between creative strategy and audience targeting. Paid campaigns outperformed expectations, while organic traffic growth slowed slightly due to reduced posting cadence. The marketing team demonstrated strong progress in optimizing ad spend, setting up for continued growth in Q4.\n\n---\n\n## Performance Metrics\n\n| Metric | Score (1–10) | Commentary |\n|--------|---------------|------------|\n| Campaign ROI | 8.5 | Paid campaigns achieved a 4.6x return, driven by optimized targeting and strong creative testing. |\n| Conversion Rate | 7.2 | Landing page refinements led to higher conversion rates, though mobile performance lags behind desktop. |\n| Engagement Rate | 8.0 | Social content featuring leadership insights and short videos performed exceptionally well, boosting visibility. |\n| Website Traffic | 7.6 | Traffic increased 9% QoQ, primarily from organic search improvements and refreshed content. |\n\n---\n\n## Key Findings\n- Campaign ROI reached its highest level in the past year.  \n- Engagement spiked on thought-leadership video content.  \n- Lead volume rose, but conversion-to-opportunity rates dipped.  \n- Organic traffic continues to be the top-performing acquisition channel.  \n- Paid search performance varies widely by region.\n\n---\n\n## Recommendations\n- Reallocate underperforming ad spend to top-performing audience segments.  \n- Prioritize mobile landing page optimization to improve conversions.  \n- Increase production of leadership and video content for social channels.  \n- Implement automated nurture workflows for MQL follow-up.  \n- Conduct a creative performance audit to identify ad fatigue early."
            }
          ]
        },
