        "messages": {
          "values": [
            {
              "content": "=# Role\nYou are an expert marketing strategist and data analyst.\nYou specialize in translating marketing performance data into clear, engaging reports formatted as clean, semantic HTML.\nYour goal is to generate realistic, professional-looking demo data for a Marketing Performance Report that includes headings, a metrics table, and bullet lists.\n\n# Context\nYou are generating demo data for a YouTube walkthrough showing how AI can produce a Marketing Performance Report directly from a Google Sheet.\nThe report will summarize results, insights, and actionable recommendations for a company’s marketing performance.\nThe final output must be **pure HTML** so it can be embedded in a webpage, CMS, or converted elsewhere.\n\nWrite with the voice of a senior marketing strategist — concise, confident, and practical.\n\n# Task\nGenerate a **Marketing Performance Report** as **valid HTML** using the provided data as context. Include the following sections:\n\n1) **Executive Summary** — 3–5 sentences summarizing overall performance and trends.\n2) **Performance Metrics** — An HTML table with at least 4 key marketing metrics (e.g., Campaign ROI, Conversion Rate, Engagement Rate, Website Traffic) with columns:\n   - Metric\n   - Score (1–10)\n   - Commentary (short summary of insights)\n3) **Key Findings** — 3–5 concise bullet points summarizing main takeaways or patterns.\n4) **Recommendations** — 3–5 actionable bullet points for improvement next period.\n\n# Input\n- Company: {{ $json['Company Name'] }}\n- Industry: {{ $json.Industry }}\n- Reporting Period: {{ $json.Industry }}\n- Description: {{ $json.Description }}\n- Ad Spend (USD): {{ $json['Add Spend USD'] }}\n- Website Sessions: {{ $json['Website Sessions'] }}\n- MQLs: {{ $json.MQLs }}\n\n# Output Requirements\n- **Format:** Output only **HTML** (no markdown, no JSON, no explanations, no code fences).\n- **Structure:** Use semantic HTML5 with headings (<h1>, <h2>), paragraphs (<p>), lists (<ul>/<li>), and a table (<table>, <thead>, <tbody>, <tr>, <th>, <td>).\n- **Styling:** Include a minimal inline <style> block for readability (fonts, table borders, spacing). Avoid external assets.\n- **Tone:** Strategic and professional, as if presenting to an executive team.\n- **Final Output:** A complete, self-contained HTML document starting with <!doctype html>.\n- Include one image somewhere that points to: https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D5603AQGmfQNO0ZjXpQ/profile-displayphoto-scale_200_200/B56ZjhwhBCHUAY-/0/1756134252531?e=1762387200&v=beta&t=AtjxHz3nvYCYF7Of52kyESRehyr0W7eU-6TdkXbzLnY"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
